      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "`Mire Triton` resolved. I milled two `Swamp`s (lucky, no spells lost). Life is 4.\n\
I have 4 `Plains` untapped.\n\
I am holding `Divine Verdict` {3}{W} (Wait, `Divine Verdict` costs {3}{W}. I have 4 `Plains` untapped, so {W}{W}{W}{W}. Yes, I can cast it.)\n\
My plan is to hold up `Divine Verdict`.\n\
I have `Valorous Stance` too.\n\
I will pass the turn and wait for their attack.\n\
\n\
Do not attack with `Tithebearer Giant`. `Visionary` (2/1) is sick, so can't attack anyway?\n\
Wait, `Lightning Visionary` is listed as `sick`.\n\
If it's sick, it can't attack next turn? (Unless it has haste, which it doesn't).\n\
Wait, earlier I said \"Visionary attacks me for 2\".\n\
If `Visionary` is sick NOW (Turn 7 Main), it was just cast?\n\
Looking at previous turn state: `Turn 7 COMBAT... bf=[... Lightning Visionary 3/2 (sick) ...]`.\n\
Wait, they cast it in their main phase Turn 7?\n\
Yes.\n\
Then it will NOT be sick on their NEXT turn (Turn 8).\n\
So next turn they attack with `Noble` and `Visionary`.\n\
Plan holds: `Divine Verdict` on `Noble`, Block `Visionary` with `Giant`. (Or block with `Mire Triton` if I want to trade deathtouch? No, `Giant` eats `Visionary` for free).\n\
Wait, `Visionary` has Prowess.\n\
If they cast a spell, `Visionary` becomes 3/2 or bigger.\n\
If `Giant` blocks (4/5), `Visionary` needs +3 power to trade. That's 3 spells. Unlikely with 1 card in hand.\n\
But if they use removal on `Giant`? `Mugging` is sorcery speed. `Sure Strike` is instant.\n\
If they have `Sure Strike` (+3/+0 First Strike), `Visionary` becomes 6/2 First Strike?\n\
3/2 base + 3 = 6.\n\
Before damage: `Visionary` 6/2 First Strike deals 6 to `Giant`. `Giant` dies.\n\
`Giant` never hits back.\n\
So `Giant` dies for free.\n\
But I have `Divine Verdict`.\n\
I can Verdict the `Visionary` instead?\n\
If `Noble` attacks (flying, 2 dmg). `Visionary` attacks (ground, 2 dmg).\n\
If I block `Visionary`. They cast `Sure Strike`.\n\
I cast `Divine Verdict` on `Visionary`.\n\
`Visionary` dies. `Sure Strike` fizzles.\n\
`Noble` hits me for 2. Trigger from `Visionary` death (-1 life).\n\
Result: I take 2 + 1 = 3 dmg.\n\
Start 4 -> 1 life. Surviving.\n\
\n\
What if I `Verdict` the `Noble`?\n\
`Noble` dies. Trigger (-1 life).\n\
`Visionary` is blocked by `Giant`.\n\
They cast `Sure Strike`. `Visionary` kills `Giant`. `Giant` dies.\n\
`Giant` trigger (-1 life)? No, `Giant` trigger is on enter. But `Giant` dying triggers... nothing.\n\
Wait, `Noble` is dead. Does `Noble` see `Giant` die?\n\
If `Noble` dies in declare blockers step, it is gone before damage step.\n\
So `Noble` does NOT see `Giant` die.\n\
So I take -1 from `Noble` death.\n\
Zero from `Noble` combat.\n\
Zero from `Visionary` combat (blocked).\n\
My `Giant` dies.\n\
I end up at 3 life.\n\
But I lose my 4/5.\n\
\n\
Which is better?\n\
A) `Verdict` `Visionary` in response to trick. Keep `Giant`. Take `Noble` hit. (1 life left).\n\
B) `Verdict` `Noble`. Lose `Giant`. Take no combat damage. (3 life left).\n\
3 life is safer than 1.\n\
But keeping a 4/5 is huge.\n\
Also they only have 1 card. If it's NOT pump, `Giant` eats `Visionary`.\n\
If I `Verdict` `Noble`, `Giant` eats `Visionary` safely assuming no trick.\n\
If they have a trick, `Giant` might die.\n\
Killing `Noble` removes the drain effect which is the biggest threat.\n\
Killing `Noble` is priority.\n\
So plan: Hold up `Verdict`. Kill `Noble` if it attacks. Block `Visionary` with `Giant`.\n\
\n\
Final Check:\n\
Pass turn.\n\
\n\
