      "player": "Gem3P ESPN",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "They attacked with both `Falkenrath Noble` (2/2 Flying) and `Lightning Visionary` (2/1).\n\
I am at 4 life.\n\
`Noble` is flying, I cannot block it.\n\
`Visionary` is ground, I can block it with `Tithebearer Giant` (4/5) or `Mire Triton` (2/1 Deathtouch).\n\
\n\
This is the moment for `Divine Verdict`.\n\
I need to kill `Falkenrath Noble` to stop the drain trigger and the flying damage.\n\
Wait, if I kill `Noble` NOW (Declare Attackers step), `Noble` dies. Trigger happens.\n\
I lose 1 life (4 -> 3).\n\
`Noble` is gone. So no combat damage from `Noble`.\n\
The only attacker left is `Lightning Visionary`.\n\
I can block `Visionary` in the Declare Blockers step (coming up next).\n\
If I block `Visionary` with `Giant` (4/5), `Visionary` (2/1) dies. `Giant` lives.\n\
Does `Noble` trigger on `Visionary`'s death?\n\
NO, because `Noble` died in Declare Attackers step. It's not on the battlefield when `Visionary` dies in Combat Damage step.\n\
So I take -1 life total from this combat.\n\
I survive at 3 life.\n\
This is optimal.\n\
\n\
Wait, `Valorous Stance` is also an option.\n\
\"Destroy target creature with toughness 4 or greater.\"\n\
`Noble` is 2/2. `Visionary` is 2/1. No targets for destroy.\n\
\"Target creature gains indestructible.\"\n\
Not useful for removing attackers.\n\
\n\
