Graveyard: `Valorous Stance`, `Mire Triton`.\n\
Hand: `Archfiend's Vessel`, `Goremand`.\n\
I'm in a good spot now.\n\
`Skyhunter Patrol` will untap next turn and dominate the air.\n\
`Goremand` next turn will sacrifice `Skyhunter` or `Giant`? No, maybe `Archfiend's Vessel` if I can get it back?\n\
Wait. `Archfiend's Vessel` says: \"When {this} enters, if it entered from your graveyard or you cast it from your graveyard, exile it. If you do, create a 5/5 black Demon creature token with flying.\"\n\
I don't have recursion in hand right now. (`Reanimate` is in GY).\n\
So `Archfiend's Vessel` is just a 1/1 lifelink.\n\
If I play it next turn ({B}), I have 5 mana left. `Goremand` is 6 mana.\n\
So I can't cast both next turn.\n\
So I can play `Vessel` as a chump blocker or `Goremand` fodder?\n\
`Goremand` needs sacrifice as *additional cost*.\n\
I can sacrifice `Vessel` to `Goremand`. `Goremand` resolves. Opponent sacrifices a creature.\n\
Allows me to upgrade 1/1 to 5/5 (Goremand).\n\
And if I ever reanimate `Vessel`, I get a 5/5 demon.\n\
So putting `Vessel` in GY (via `Goremand` sac) is good setup for later recursion.\n\
But for now, I pass turn.\n\
\n\
