But I only need {1}{W}.\n\
I have 4 Plains + 1 Swamp + 1 Heath (W or B).\n\
If I use Heath for {W}, I have {W} + 4 Plains + 1 Swamp.\n\
If I use Heath for {B}, I have {B} + 4 Plains + 1 Swamp.\n\
It doesn't matter much unless I need BB later.\n\
`Goremand` needs BB.\n\
`Vessel` needs B.\n\
I have 1 Swamp.\n\
So I should probably keep `Heath` available for B if possible, or tap it for B now.\n\
Wait, I am casting `Kami` ({1}{W}).\n\
The autodetection selected `Thriving Heath` to pay for it?\n\
That's odd. Usually it taps basics first.\n\
Maybe it wants to save the Swamp for `Vessel`?\n\
So if I tap Heath now, I should tap it for W or B?\n\
If I tap for W, I use Heath + 1 Plains. Remaining: 3 Plains + 1 Swamp.\n\
Next spell `Vessel` ({B}). use Swamp. Remaining: 3 Plains.\n\
If I tap for B, I use Heath + 1 Plains. Remaining: 3 Plains + 1 Swamp.\n\
Wait. `Kami` costs {1}{W}.\n\
