So I can't do both in one turn unless I have 8 mana. I have 6.\n\
So choice is: `Goremand` OR `Patrol` + pass (or just attack).\n\
`Goremand` is better clock.\n\
So sequence:\n\
Attack with all.\n\
Postcombat: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel` (or `Kami`).\n\
Sac `Vessel` (1/1) seems best.\n\
But `Vessel` has lifelink.\n\
Opponent at 2 life.\n\
Next turn they need to deal 3 damage to me.\n\
If I have blockers...\n\
`Giant` and `Kami` will stay back?\n\
No, I attack with ALL.\n\
They are tapped.\n\
If opponent has a haste creature or removal + creature?\n\
They have 9 lands.\n\
If they cast a big haste threat...\n\
They have Black/Red.\n\
Likely removal.\n\
If they remove my blockers, I die?\n\
Wait. I am at 3 life.\n\
If I attack with all, I am tapped out.\n\
If they drop a 3/3 Haste, I die.\n\
Is there a 3/3 Haste in M21?\n\
`Volcanic Geyser` (X spell)? `Shock`?\n\
`Pitchburn Devils`?\n\
`Hellkite Punisher`?\n\
Maybe I should hold back `Kami` or `Giant`?\n\
`Skyhunter` has Flying, hard to block.\n\
`Giant` (4/5).\n\
`Vessel` (1/1 Lifelink).\n\
If I attack with `Vessel`, I gain 1 life -> 4 life.\n\
That's safer.\n\
Opponent has no hand (last check), but drew 1 card.\n\
Unless they sandbagged.\n\
They played Mountain last turn.\n\
So they have 1 unknown card.\n\
It's risky to be tapped out at 3 life vs Red.\n\
I should keep `Giant` back?\n\
`Giant` is 4/5. tough blocker.\n\
If I attack with `Skyhunter` (2), `Kami` (2), `Vessel` (1).\n\
Total 5 damage. Opponent -> 6.\n\
I gain 1 life -> 4.\n\
Then Main 2: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel`?\n\
Or sac `Kami`?\n\
Sac `Vessel` (tapped).\n\
`Goremand` is 5/5 blocker (Flying).\n\
So I will have `Goremand` (untapped) and `Giant` (untapped).\n\
That's very safe.\n\
And opponent at 6 life.\n\
Next turn `Goremand` (5) + `Giant` (4) is lethal.\n\
Wait. `Goremand` flies. 5 damage.\n\
`Skyhunter` flies. 2 damage.\n\
Total 7 flying damage.\n\
Lethal.\n\
So I don't need to attack with `Giant` this turn to set up lethal.\n\
Attacking with `Skyhunter` (2) + `Vessel` (1) + `Kami` (2) puts them to 6.\n\
Next turn Flying (5+2=7) kills them.\n\
So `Giant` can stay back.\n\
And `Kami`?\n\
If I sac `Kami` to `Goremand`?\n\
I have `Vessel` (1/1).\n\
`Goremand` trigger: Opponent sacs creature. (Whiff).\n\
If I sac `Kami` (2/2) instead of `Vessel` (1/1).\n\
I keep `Vessel` (1/1 lifelink).\n\
`Vessel` is better to sac because it's smaller?\n\
But `Vessel` gains life.\n\
If I attack with `Vessel`, it taps.\n\
I sac it post-combat.\n\
I gained 1 life (important!).\n\
So plan:\n\
Attack with `Skyhunter`, `Kami`, `Vessel`.\n\
Blocked? No blockers.\n\
Damage: 5. Opponent 11 -> 6.\n\
I gain 1 life -> 4.\n\
Post-combat: Cast `Goremand`, sac `Vessel`.\n\
Board: `Goremand` (5/5 F/T), `Giant` (4/5), `Skyhunter` (2/3 tapped), `Kami` (2/2 tapped).\n\
Opponent Turn: Facing 4 life, 5/5 blocker, 4/5 blocker.\n\
My Turn: Attack with `Goremand` + `Skyhunter` = 7 Flying damage. Lethal.\n\
Strategy sound.\n\
Attacking with `Giant` is greedy and risks haste lethal.\n\
So: Pass priority to combat.\n\
\n\
Action: `choose_action(choice=\"no\")`.\n\
