Why would I give their creature +7/+7? To kill my Giant? No thanks.\n\
Wait, can I target my blocked creature? No, blocked is not \"blocking\". Blocking means declared as a blocker.\n\
So `Righteousness` is useless here unless I want to buff their blocker. Lol. no.\n\
\n\
So I pass priority.\n\
Unless they have a fog or something, they are dead.\n\
If they kill Goremand, Skyhunter hits for lethal.\n\
The only way they survive is a mass removal or something crazy.\n\
\n\
Pass.\n\
\n\
One final chat: \"AND THAT'S THE BALL GAME! OFFENSE EXECUTES PERFECTLY!\"\n\
\n\
Wait, I don't need to overdo the chat. Just pass.\n\
\n\
Action: `choose_action(choice=\"no\")`\n\
\n\
(The previous `choice=\"p59\"` error `Object p59 not found in current choices` was because by then attackers were already locked in or step advanced? The board shows combat happening. So attackers were declared successfully somehow, maybe by the previous call despite the error message? The state shows \"Combat: Goremand -> ...\". So yes, attacking happened.)\n\
\n\
I pass.\n\
\n\
